pacing='# Pacing notes\\n\\n60.000 seconds; 24fps; 1,440 frames. Intervals are start-inclusive/end-exclusive. All beat timings below are local to the shot. Silence means no speech; room tone continues until 55.000. Locked camera throughout.\\n\\n| Shot | Master interval / seconds | Framing | Action and exact holds | Cut out |\\n|---|---|---|---|---|\\n'
for n,t,d,f,b in shots:
 cut='Straight cut' if n<6 else ('Hard cut to black; all audio cuts' if n==6 else ('Hard title appearance' if n==7 else 'End on title; no fade'))
 pacing+=f'| {n:02} | {t:02}–{t+d:02} / {d}s | {f} | {b} | {cut} |\\n'
pacing+='\\nFielder sits at Dan’s dining table; his overnight bag and folded sleeping bag suggest he has effectively moved in. Dan remains bureaucratically serene. Roy occupies the same interview chair on a separate occasion: tired eyes, immediate certainty. No reaction punches, inserts, ominous gestures, or comic stress.\\n\\nThe opening pauses establish patience; the access question gives the domestic stillness moral weight. Roy briefly breaks the delayed-answer pattern. Dan then reduces demolition to a parking specification. Shot 06 has the longest uninterrupted speech-free hold: eight seconds. Maintain lens contact, ordinary breathing, and natural blinking. The black gap separates the stare from a four-second static title without musical relief.\\n'
P.joinpath('PACING_NOTES.md').write_text(pacing)
script='# Script\\n\\nAll characters are fictional. FIELDER is an original filmmaker-interviewer, with no real-person likeness or impersonation. DAN is the wealthy CEO of Pinterest in this fictional continuity. He demolished a community food bank for an oversized Tesla-style parking space for his own sedan. ROY is his loyal associate and friend, visibly carrying the strain of that loyalty. The demolition is a settled fact.\\n\\nSoft, ordinary conversational delivery; no irony, smiles, comic timing, or ominous performance. All pauses follow PACING_NOTES.md. Voices stay close and dry.\\n\\n| Shot | Master seconds | Exact dialogue |\\n|---|---|---|\\n'
for n,t,d,f,b in shots:
 for who,line,a,z in lines.get(n,[]): script+=f'| {n:02} | {t+a:06.3f}–{t+z:06.3f} | {who}: {line} |\\n'
script+='\\nNo other speech, narration, captions, or improvised vocalizations. Shots 07–08 are digitally silent. Dan maintains lens contact throughout shots 05–06, including across the cut.\\n'
P.joinpath('SCRIPT.md').write_text(script)
P.joinpath('TITLES.md').write_text('''# Titles

24fps, 60 seconds. Add final typography in post.

| Shot | Master seconds | Zero-based frames, inclusive | Exact text | Treatment |
|---|---|---|---|---|
| 07 | 55.000–56.000 | 1320–1343 | None | Solid #000000; hard cut from stare. |
| 08 | 56.000–60.000 | 1344–1439 | YOU CAN SEE ANYTHING | One centered line; hard appearance; static to end. |

Minimal independent-documentary typography with A24-like restraint: regular neutral neo-grotesque sans serif, uppercase; no studio logo imitation. Helvetica Neue Regular or metrically similar substitute. Off-white #E6E4DF on black #000000. At 1920×1080: 64px type, 0.08em tracking, optical center at 50% horizontal / 50% vertical, at least 12% side margins. Scale proportionally. No secondary cards, billing, release date, animation, texture, fade, or audio accent. Last frame retains title.
''')
P.joinpath('MUSIC_CUES.md').write_text('''# Music and sound cues

48kHz stereo PCM; 60s master matches picture. No swell, pulse, sting, or answer accents. Dry centered dialogue around −23 LUFS short-term. Do not normalize quiet passages upward. Gains below are dBFS peak relative to a unit-peak source after filtering and before envelope. Final true peak below −3dBTP.

| Cue | Shots | Master entry–exit / duration | Fundamental / source | Envelope / gain |
|---|---|---|---|---|
| R1 room tone | 01–06 | 0.000–55.000 / 55s | Seeded white noise, bandpass 100–3000Hz; no fundamental | 0.25s linear attack, sustain, hard cut at 55.000; peak −48dBFS |
| H1 distant electrical hum | 01–06 | 0.000–55.000 / 55s | 60Hz sine | 0.25s linear attack, sustain, hard cut at 55.000; −66dBFS |
| D1 low drone | 03–05 | 18.000–40.000 / 22s | 43.65Hz sine, F1 | 6s raised-cosine attack, 10s sustain, 6s raised-cosine release; −42dBFS |
| P1 single piano-like note | 02 | 11.000–14.000 / 3s | 174.61Hz, F3; additive recipe below | 0.008s attack; exponential decay τ=0.65s; final 0.15s linear release; −35dBFS |
| P2 single piano-like note | 05 | 40.000–42.000 / 2s | 130.81Hz, C3; additive recipe below | 0.008s attack; exponential decay τ=0.45s; final 0.15s linear release; −38dBFS |
| S1 digital silence | 07–08 | 55.000–60.000 / 5s | Zero samples; no fundamental | −∞dBFS |

Drone attack E(t)=(1−cos(πt/6))/2 for first 6s; release mirrors this in final 6s. No modulation or harmonics. Piano-like synthesis: sum zero-phase sine partials at f, 2f, 3f, 4f with relative amplitudes 1, 0.35, 0.12, 0.04; normalize composite peak to unity, then apply gain and envelope. Attack rises linearly to one in 0.008s; thereafter decay exp(−(t−0.008)/τ). Multiply final 0.15s by linear ramp to zero. No pedal or reverb.

FFmpeg synthesis: "'`anoisesrc` with fixed seed 2718 and `highpass`/`lowpass` for R1; `aevalsrc` for sine and additive sources, with sample-accurate envelopes. Generate at listed durations; place using `adelay` at 0ms (R1/H1), 18000ms (D1), 11000ms (P1), 40000ms (P2). Mix with `amix=normalize=0`. Retain natural breathing and faint fabric movement before 55s; no added Foley. Shot 06 has no score. Trim all production sound at sample 2640000; samples 2640000–2879999 are zero. No tail crosses into black. Do not gate the earlier speech pauses.
'"''')
D='a fictional man in his late 30s with light skin, short neat dark-brown hair with slight recession at the temples, clean-shaven, average build, calm neutral intelligent expression, steady eyes, wearing a dark olive-green practical rain jacket with the collar slightly up and a gray crew-neck sweater underneath'
R='a fictional man in his early 40s with light skin, short slightly wavy sandy-blond hair, light stubble on the jaw, slightly heavier than average build, tired but kind eyes, neutral grounded expression, wearing a charcoal-gray knit sweater over a navy collared shirt'
F='a fictional man in his early 40s with medium-brown skin, closely cropped black hair, clean-shaven, slender build, long oval face, quiet attentive eyes, neutral unreadable expression, wearing a plain slate-blue button-down shirt with sleeves buttoned at the wrists, an original deadpan documentary filmmaker-interviewer with no likeness to any real person'
L=\"a quiet, plain, softly lit dining room inside Dan's suburban house, pale warm-gray walls, a bare oak table, mismatched upholstered chairs, a broad window with thin cream curtains, a folded sleeping bag and an overnight bag against the far wall suggesting the interviewer has effectively moved in, domestic slightly too intimate proportions, minimal documentary crew footprint, no visible crew or lighting equipment\"
S='photorealistic live-action cinematography, 24fps, overcast Pacific Northwest suburb, natural lighting, restrained muted color grade, no cartoon effects, no exaggerated expressions, everyone behaves completely seriously'
continuity=f'DAN: {D}\\n\\nROY: {R}\\n\\nFIELDER: {F}\\n\\nINTERVIEW ROOM: {L}'
refs={1:'FIELDER ref',2:'DAN ref',3:'DAN ref; FIELDER ref for offscreen voice continuity only',4:'ROY ref; FIELDER ref for offscreen voice continuity only',5:'DAN ref',6:'DAN ref; FIELDER ref for offscreen voice continuity only',7:'None',8:'None'}
prompts='# Clip prompts\\n\\n16:9, 1920×1080 delivery. Each prompt is independent. Repeated cast/location descriptions are continuity metadata: render only the explicitly named visible subject; other cast remain absent. For graphic plates, all cast and location metadata are non-rendering. Reference portraits are future inputs, not generated by this document. Replace generated dialogue in post if needed to preserve exact line windows and holds.\\n'
for n,t,d,f,b in shots:
 visible=('Only '+('FIELDER' if n==1 else 'ROY' if n==4 else 'DAN')+' visible. '+f+'. Plain domestic setting, softly lit by curtained window; locked tripod; no subtitles, logos, or crew. '+('Overnight bag and folded sleeping bag softly visible behind FIELDER. ' if n==1 else '')) if n<7 else ('Pure #000000 graphic plate; no people, room, texture, or objects. '+('No text.' if n==7 else 'Final title: YOU CAN SEE ANYTHING, centered single line, off-white regular neutral sans serif, 64px at 1080p, 0.08em tracking.'))
 for kind in ['Still-image','Video']:
  if kind=='Still-image': action='Use a neutral silent instant; ordinary expression, no theatrical emotion.' if n<7 else ('Render exact title as a typography mockup; final type will be replaced in post.' if n==8 else 'Solid black, no lettering.')
  else:
   action=f'Exactly {d}s. Local timeline: {b} '
   for who,line,a,z in lines.get(n,[]): action+=f'{a}–{z}s {who}: “{line}” '
   action+=('Soft dry conversational voices; no score baked in, no camera movement. Natural blinking and breathing; no ironic emphasis.' if n<7 else 'No generated audio or fades. '+('Generate a clean black base plate without lettering; composite final title in post per TITLES.md.' if n==8 else ''))
  if kind=='Still-image': prompts+=f'\\n## Shot {n:02} — {d}s\\n\\nReference portraits: {refs[n]}.\\n'
  prompts+=f'\\n### {kind} prompt\\n\\n{continuity}\\n\\n{S}\\n\\n16:9. {visible} {action}\\n'
P.joinpath('CLIP_PROMPTS.md').write_text(prompts)
assert sum(s[2] for s in shots)==60
